# Audit Report -- Phase 290: gate seal-tag push on CI success for the tagged SHA (GH #482)

**Verdict**: PASS

**Target**: docs/plan-qor-phase290-tag-push-ci-gate.md

Binding gates executed: prompt_injection_canaries --mask-code-blocks --strict rc=0;
prose_test_lint --enforce rc=0 (69 exempted, 0 unexplained); publication_boundary_lint
0 findings; plan_grep_lint 0 citations (no Locked Decisions block, matching the
phase163 template precedent); substantiate_gates ladder unchanged (10 gates, order
verified); audit_risk_score: option_b_required=false (no author-momentum signal).

GH #482's own "Scope note" fixes the plan's boundary: the interaction between two
individually-correct controls (Step 9.5.5 tag-by-exact-SHA, Step 9.7 ancestor-only
reachability) is the defect, not either control. The fix composes rather than
replaces: qor.scripts.tag_ci_gate.evaluate delegates to the already-tested
release_ci_gate.evaluate for the CI half and takes the caller's own git merge-base
result for the ancestor half.

TDD verified directly: tests/test_tag_ci_gate.py (8 cases) and
tests/test_substantiate_tag_ci_gate_wiring.py (3 cases, anchored-prose with
strip-and-fail negatives) confirmed red before the implementation existed, green
after, re-run twice for determinism. Full suite: 3523 passed / 4 skipped / 4
deselected, run twice, deterministic.

One real regression caught and fixed pre-audit: the Step 9.7 prose addition pushed
SKILL.md past test_ladder_rewrite_left_usable_slack's 2700 B floor (file was already
within 2 B of the floor pre-change). Trimmed by moving rationale to
references/release-and-tag-timing.md and compacting the bash block from nested
if/else to a single &&-gated push; final size 37223 B, 2713 B slack.

Governance/planning drift found, not this phase's to fix: qor/dist/*/manifest.json
on main records sha256 values for several unrelated variant files that do not match
those files' actual committed content; manifest.json is excluded from
check_variant_drift's comparison by design. Pre-existing, unrelated to GH #482.

**Required next action**: /qor-implement (already complete; proceeding directly to seal).
